---
// Lesson Detail Component
---
<aside class="lesson-detail-panel" id="detailPanel" role="complementary" aria-labelledby="detailTitle">
  <div class="detail-badge-row">
    <span class="part-tag" id="detailPartTag">Part 0: Language Basics</span>
    <span style="font-size: 0.75rem; color: #94a3b8; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;" id="detailId">#B1</span>
  </div>

  <h1 class="lesson-title" id="detailTitle">Variables, := & Zero Values</h1>
  <p class="lesson-desc" id="detailDesc">
    In JS, variables can start undefined and change types at runtime. In Go, every variable has a static type and a default 'Zero Value' (0, "", false, or nil). The := operator automatically infers types.
  </p>

  <div class="card-box node-box" role="region" aria-label="Node.js Code Comparison">
    <div class="node-header-row">
      <span class="node-tag">🟢 Node.js Equivalent</span>
      <button id="copyNodeBtn" class="copy-snippet-btn" onclick="copyNodeSnippet()" aria-label="Copy Node.js snippet to clipboard">📋 Copy</button>
    </div>
    <div class="node-code" id="detailNodeCode" tabindex="0" role="textbox" aria-readonly="true" aria-label="Node.js code example">let name = 'Gopher'; let count = 0; let active = false;</div>
  </div>

  <div class="card-box go-why-box" role="region" aria-label="Go Mental Model Rationale">
    <div class="go-why-title"><span aria-hidden="true">💡</span> The Go Mental Model</div>
    <p class="go-why-desc" id="detailGoWhy">
      Zero values eliminate 'Cannot read properties of undefined' crashes. Variables in Go are never in an uninitialized state.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-nav-footer" role="navigation" aria-label="Lesson Step Navigation">
    <button id="btnPrevLesson" class="nav-lesson-btn" onclick="navigateLesson(-1)" aria-label="Navigate to previous lesson">← Previous</button>
    <button id="btnNextLesson" class="nav-lesson-btn primary" onclick="navigateLesson(1)" aria-label="Navigate to next lesson">Next Lesson →</button>
  </div>
</aside>
